 Pre-registered hypotheses (ex-post-explicit, per N3):
   H0: v2 is doing subgraph census →
       at saturation: within ≈ cross (both high or both moderate)
       at low budget: within ≈ cross (both noisy/low)

   H1: substrate-sensitive emergence →
       at saturation: within > 0.7 AND cross < 0.4
       at low budget: within stays > 0.5 AND cross < 0.4

 KEY DISCRIMINATOR: under LOW budget, does within stay HIGH?
   If yes → substrate fingerprint is structurally real (H1)
   If no  → it was just census saturation (H0)

